1
00:00:02,134 --> 00:00:04,670
So with arrays and sets, we had a detailed

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:07,222
look at our list data structures in

3
00:00:07,335 --> 00:00:10,111
JavaScript. So data structures that simply

4
00:00:10,208 --> 00:00:12,535
help us with managing lists of data.

5
00:00:13,257 --> 00:00:16,291
Now it's time for objects. And an object can

6
00:00:16,387 --> 00:00:16,917
look like this.

7
00:00:17,768 --> 00:00:20,127
We can create it with this shortcut here,

8
00:00:20,175 --> 00:00:22,487
with this shorthand notation in JavaScript

9
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:23,514
with the curly braces.

10
00:00:24,332 --> 00:00:27,077
And objects can have key-value pairs like

11
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:29,244
name and age, which store a string and a

12
00:00:29,244 --> 00:00:32,069
number. But objects also and that is

13
00:00:32,069 --> 00:00:34,833
important to keep in mind, can have methods

14
00:00:35,026 --> 00:00:36,601
attached to them. They can have

15
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:39,268
functionality that's part of the object,

16
00:00:39,589 --> 00:00:41,742
like this greet method, which then in turn

17
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,169
is actually able to interact with the

18
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,000
key-value pairs, with the so-called

19
00:00:46,097 --> 00:00:47,816
properties of the object.

20
00:00:48,989 --> 00:00:51,544
Now, objects in general are unordered

21
00:00:51,576 --> 00:00:53,086
key-value pairs of data.

22
00:00:53,986 --> 00:00:56,798
The element access is done with help of the

23
00:00:56,798 --> 00:00:58,871
key name. So of the property name. For

24
00:00:58,887 --> 00:01:02,469
example, to get the age value, you use age

25
00:01:02,807 --> 00:01:03,498
as an identifier.

26
00:01:04,574 --> 00:01:07,048
Objects are not really iterable. There is

27
00:01:07,144 --> 00:01:09,795
the for-in loop which is built for objects,

28
00:01:09,956 --> 00:01:11,900
but you won't be able to use the for-of

29
00:01:11,964 --> 00:01:15,000
loop. You won't be able to access the values

30
00:01:15,032 --> 00:01:16,960
with help of some index or anything like

31
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:17,201
that.

32
00:01:18,229 --> 00:01:21,747
Keys are unique, values are not. So every

33
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:25,377
key name must only appear once You can't

34
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:28,184
have 2 age properties in the same object. If

35
00:01:28,184 --> 00:01:30,205
you do, the second property would simply

36
00:01:30,349 --> 00:01:32,338
override the first one, but you can

37
00:01:32,515 --> 00:01:34,760
absolutely have the same value multiple

38
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:38,032
times. If you store the number 31 for age

39
00:01:38,305 --> 00:01:39,059
and also for

40
00:01:39,652 --> 00:01:42,379
oldAge or some other property name, that

41
00:01:42,379 --> 00:01:43,534
would be perfectly fine.

42
00:01:44,544 --> 00:01:46,645
Now, one other important thing is that the

43
00:01:46,645 --> 00:01:50,014
keys for your properties actually have to be

44
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:52,917
strings, numbers, or symbols in JavaScript.

45
00:01:53,687 --> 00:01:56,028
Most of the time, this is all what you want,

46
00:01:56,173 --> 00:01:58,450
but it is worth noting that your keys, for

47
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:01,803
example, may not be objects themselves. So

48
00:02:01,803 --> 00:02:04,625
it has to be something like name or 1 or a

49
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:05,123
symbol,

50
00:02:05,876 --> 00:02:07,945
but it's not allowed to be an object or an

51
00:02:07,994 --> 00:02:08,314
array.

52
00:02:09,646 --> 00:02:09,774
Now,

53
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:12,485
objects in general therefore can be

54
00:02:12,485 --> 00:02:15,484
summarized as data structures or as

55
00:02:15,676 --> 00:02:19,574
constructs that can store data but that also

56
00:02:19,606 --> 00:02:22,380
can contain extra functionalities. Namely

57
00:02:22,637 --> 00:02:23,582
the methods you can add.

58
00:02:24,159 --> 00:02:25,825
In addition, of course, it's also worth

59
00:02:25,921 --> 00:02:28,774
noting that objects in JavaScript have this

60
00:02:28,822 --> 00:02:30,905
prototypes thing, that you can use

61
00:02:30,905 --> 00:02:33,933
constructor functions to create objects, and

62
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:36,433
that you got all these extra features on top

63
00:02:36,497 --> 00:02:39,413
of objects, so to say. So it's really more

64
00:02:39,862 --> 00:02:41,160
than just a data structure.

65
00:02:41,785 --> 00:02:44,253
Nonetheless, objects in JavaScript are the

66
00:02:44,253 --> 00:02:47,473
main key-value store you use whenever you

67
00:02:47,473 --> 00:02:49,899
don't need a list but well, a key data

68
00:02:49,899 --> 00:02:51,768
store. So whenever you wanna group data

69
00:02:51,833 --> 00:02:52,284
together,

70
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,733
let's also see objects in code therefore.

71
00:02:55,942 --> 00:02:59,135
Again, back in an empty app.js file, we can

72
00:02:59,168 --> 00:03:00,717
create our person object

73
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:03,719
where we have the firstName, let's say,

74
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:06,979
which is Max and the age, which is 31 and

75
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:09,257
hobbies, which is an array, let's say, with

76
00:03:09,257 --> 00:03:09,838
sports

77
00:03:10,371 --> 00:03:11,244
and cooking.

78
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:15,761
Now, as I mentioned, you won't be able to

79
00:03:15,857 --> 00:03:17,752
use the for-of loop here

80
00:03:18,426 --> 00:03:20,931
and console.log the element.

81
00:03:21,637 --> 00:03:24,255
If you do that, you will get an error that

82
00:03:24,367 --> 00:03:27,418
person is not iterable so that you can't use

83
00:03:27,418 --> 00:03:27,466
it.

84
00:03:28,461 --> 00:03:30,260
And you also can't access

85
00:03:31,592 --> 00:03:34,370
elements by index. This will not give you an

86
00:03:34,563 --> 00:03:36,875
error, but instead now this would simply

87
00:03:36,891 --> 00:03:40,600
look for a key named 0, and we have no 0 key

